From cbcd1f23ca5e61a8bc92ea63050e5457ff08fb21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhen XIN <lone.zen6@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 03:44:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] pinctrl: ingenic: use raw spinlock for regmap

GPIO irq_chip callbacks such as irq_set_type run while the IRQ core holds a raw descriptor lock. Ingenic register updates use regmap, whose default MMIO lock is a regular spinlock, causing lockdep to report an invalid wait context during IRQ setup.

Use regmap raw spinlock locking so GPIO register accesses are safe under the IRQ core raw lock.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
index bf94a026b5a1..de7e80e23599 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
@@ -4036,6 +4036,7 @@ static const struct regmap_config ingenic_pinctrl_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_bits = 32,
 	.val_bits = 32,
 	.reg_stride = 4,
+	.use_raw_spinlock = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id ingenic_gpio_of_matches[] __initconst = {
